{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/12675-lunars-how-i-learned-to-relax-and-love-the-inspirational-overlap","id":12675,"title":"[Lunars] How I learned to relax and love the inspirational overlap","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T05:58:35-08:00","id":12675,"title":"[Lunars] How I learned to relax and love the inspirational overlap","content":"Recently, I've come to a realization.<br /> <br /> It's <i>okay </i>that many sources of Lunar inspiration also double as inspiration for animal gods, zoanthropic demons or elementals, raksha with beastly guises, and behemoths. Many purely-human heroes can themselves be inspiration to various Exalted Hosts at once. Tolkein's Aragorn, for example, has Solar themes as a returning rightful king with superior faculties compared to the commoners, nobles and stewards of his kingdom, but he's also part of a line of kings whose potency and legitimacy are hereditary as per the Dragon-Blooded. Wizards could either be sorcerous Lawgivers with a penchant for subtetly and benign manipulation of geopolitical effects, or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> So it's a pointless waste of time to ask if Cuchulain was a Solar or Lunar, and it's meaningless to wonder if Hanuman or Sun Wukong was a monkey-god, monkey-behemoth, monkey-raksha, or monkey-Lunar. The real-world rakshasha were inspirational for the nobility of the Fair Folk, yet the Exalt called Raksi is herself patterned on them through the lense of humanity and the Lunar Host.<br /> <br /> And this is a good thing! It injects variety and mystery into the setting, allowing storytellers to spring things on players without the players always being able to immediately identify what they're dealing with today.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the <i>important</i> questions are these: &quot;If Cuchulain and Hanuman were taken as Lunar inspiration, which of their feats would make appropriate Lunar Exalted Charms or anima effects? And of those feats not appropriate to the Lunar Exalted, which would be appropriate Charms or powers for the splats which likewise share these figures as inspirational sources?&quot;<br /> <br /> And, &quot;If this figure was an Exalted human, how does that change his story and character compared to the possibility that he is an immortal spirit or a soul-eating alien monstrosity from beyond the borders of the understandable world?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T07:06:58-08:00","id":12707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/12675-lunars-how-i-learned-to-relax-and-love-the-inspirational-overlap#post12675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real-world rakshasha were inspirational for the nobility of the Fair Folk, yet the Exalt called Raksi is herself patterned on them through the lense of humanity and the Lunar Host.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also that time Lea noted that the Fair Folk cover vampire, nobility and exile markers, but not the ones that Abyssals, Dragon Blooded and Lunars do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T08:13:59-08:00","id":12742,"title":"","content":"Welcome to enlightenment, friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T10:49:47-08:00","id":12804,"title":"","content":"Agreed on all points. I enjoy discussions of &quot;Which type of entity would character X be in Creation?&quot; up until they people start insisting on One True Interpretation. I've found this baffling. As you say, all of the different types shouldn't be seen as mutually exclusive categories, but lenses designed to emphasize certain themes.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say some lenses can't be more natural fits than others. Just that undue focus on arguments about &quot;the best fit&quot; drowns out discussion of ways in which other splats do and don't fit, and what (sometimes surprising) inspiration a character might provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Verbiage. 11-17-2013, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T11:14:08-08:00","id":12821,"title":"","content":"Something profound has happened...and it is good. Either that or the body snatchers have arrived <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T11:39:24-08:00","id":12836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/12675-lunars-how-i-learned-to-relax-and-love-the-inspirational-overlap?p=12707#post12707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also that time Lea noted that the Fair Folk cover vampire, nobility and exile markers, but not the ones that Abyssals, Dragon Blooded and Lunars do.</div> </div> </div> </div> It would be interesting to see a Venn Diagram of the different areas each splat covers and in which they overlap with other splats. Of course, the qualities of &quot;nobility and exile&quot; are external conditions. The Lunars of Heaven's Reach are not exiles, and in some world the raksha might be enslaved to some other power rather than the lords of chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T12:08:15-08:00","id":12859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/12675-lunars-how-i-learned-to-relax-and-love-the-inspirational-overlap?p=12707#post12707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also that time Lea noted that the Fair Folk cover vampire, nobility and exile markers, but not the ones that Abyssals, Dragon Blooded and Lunars do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget that the Lunar overlap was also &quot;psychedelic dream tropes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T12:08:20-08:00","id":12860,"title":"","content":"I'd say part of accepting the way Exalted is written is that part of the themes of any given group are just as legitimately who they are as it is what they are.<br /> <br /> This is a pretty big thing with the Lunars, given how much they seem to be putting on their opposition to the Sidereals and the Realm.<br /> <br /> White Wolf games in general seem to have a strong focus on making character types and groups out of unexpected interactions rather than pure concepts, for the sake of some theme.<br /> <br /> Even is some people take offense at this being some kind of presentation of robots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}